verdict.fix:
The approach is right, but it needs a test-harness change too. The file is in scope (not an entry/auth file, not a test, not a gallery) and no owner rule is touched: no dependency (RN core API, already used in V2Action.tsx:115, AvailabilityForm.tsx:346 and InboxPresentation.tsx:247), no TTS (only an active TalkBack/VoiceOver speaks it; on Android RN 0.86.3 returns early when accessibility is off), no guard, read-marking or recovery changed.

1) src/ui/aiFirst/AiConversationShell.tsx: add AccessibilityInfo to the react-native import, then next to `seen`:
```
const announced = useRef<string | null>(null);
useEffect(() => {
  const fresh = p.messages.filter(message => message.fromAi && !seen.current.has(message.id)).at(-1);
  if (fresh && fresh.id !== announced.current) {
    announced.current = fresh.id;
    AccessibilityInfo.announceForAccessibility(`USKOČI: ${fresh.body}`);
  }
}, [p.messages]);
```
- Call it from an effect, not during render.
- Keep `announced` separate from `seen`. `seen` means "history at open" and drives the entrance animation at :132, so it must not be mutated.
- Leave the typing indicator alone, and do not put a live region on `streamingText`, which would speak every delta. The full reply is spoken once, when the persisted turn arrives. This also covers voice mode, whose answer block (VoiceComposer.tsx:239) has no live region either.

2) Required with it: in src/data/__tests__/ai-owned-intake-screen.test.tsx:54, add `announceForAccessibility: jest.fn()` to the AccessibilityInfo stand-in. This does not change what the test checks.

3) Regression test in src/data/__tests__/ai-conversation-layout.test.tsx:
- Hoist `const mockAnnounce = jest.fn()` and use it in the Proxy's AccessibilityInfo. The current inline `jest.fn()` is created anew on every property access, so no test can assert on it.
- Assert that history is not announced and the person's own turn is not announced.
- Assert that a newly arrived AI turn is announced once, as 'USKOČI: <body>'.
- Assert that a rerender with a new messages array does not repeat the announcement.

Verified on the scratch copy: both suites pass 113/113 with the fix, the new test fails on the original code, and tsc reports no errors in the touched files.

